      <https://w3id.org/iadopt/ont/Variable>;
    dct:description "Carbon fixation is a process found in autotrophs, usually driven by photosynthesis, whereby carbon dioxide (CO(2)) is converted into organic compounds. There are three types of carbon fixation pathways: i) C3 acid cycle; ii) C4 acid cycle; iii) CAM pathway";
    rdfs:label "Carbon fixation pathway", "Carbon fixation";
